Line 1: There's no character at position 0.
    say every 0th character of word
              ^^^
Positions start at 1: "every 2nd character" means characters 2, 4, 6 and so on.

Line 2: Something is missing after "character".
    say character of word
        ^^^^^^^^^
Say which character, like "character 1", "the first character", or "the last character".

Line 3: Something is missing after "to".
    say characters 2 to of word
                     ^^
Say where the characters end, like "characters 2 to 4 of word" or "characters 2 to the end of word".

Line 4: I expected "of" here, but found "word".
    say the first 3 characters word
                               ^^^^
Write it like "the first 3 characters of word".

Line 5: I expected "in" here, but found "word".
    say the position of "x" word
                            ^^^^
Write it like "the position of "x" in word".

Line 6: I expected "by" here, but found the text "b".
    say word with "a" replaced "b"
                               ^^^
Write it like "word with "a" replaced by "b"".

Line 7: Something is missing after "split".
    say word split ","
             ^^^^^
Did you mean "split by"?

Line 8: Something is missing after "joined".
    say names joined ", "
              ^^^^^^
Did you mean "joined with"?

Line 9: Something is missing after "without extra".
    say word without extra
             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "without extra spaces"?

Line 10: Something is missing after "without the first".
    say word without the first
             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "without the first item" or "without the first character"?

Line 11: Something is missing after "starts".
    say word starts "a"
             ^^^^^^
Did you mean "starts with"?

Line 12: Something is missing after "does not start".
    say word does not start "a"
             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "does not start with"?

Line 13: A position worked out with arithmetic needs parentheses.
    say characters 2 plus 1 to 3 of word
                     ^^^^
Write it like "character (n plus 1) of word".

Line 14: A position worked out with arithmetic needs parentheses.
    say the first n plus 1 characters of word
                    ^^^^
Write it like "character (n plus 1) of word".
